  "text_input": "Patient presented with shortness of breath, insidious in onset and gradually progressive. He also had cough with expectoration for 5 days, yellowish sputum, and low-grade intermittent fever with chills. Burning micturition and chest tightness were reported. Physical examination revealed SpO2 of 88% on room air and bilateral decreased air entry in upper lung fields. Known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Hypertension for 19 years, and dyslipidemia for 5 years. Chronic smoker for 30 years. Diagnosed with sepsis secondary to bronchopneumonia with right upper lobe fibrosis, old pulmonary tuberculosis, systemic hypertension with grade 3 hypertensive retinopathy, and type 2 diabetes mellitus with mild NPDR.",
